  # modprobe snd-cs4231
  cs4231 cs4231.0: please specify port

Create platform devices for the CHRP ISA sound nodes and bind snd-cs4231
to them, e.g. on the IBM 7043-150:

  /pci@80000000/isa@b/sound@i534: compatible "CRUS,CS4236B", "IBM0017",
  "pnpPNP,b007", reg <1 0x534 8 ...>, interrupts <5 3>, dma 0 and 1

Port and interrupt come from the node, the DMA channels from its ISA "dma"
property (5 cells per channel), which lists the capture channel first.
This gives port 0x534, irq 5, playback dma 1 and capture dma 0, measured
to work for playback and capture; irq 9 gets no interrupts and capture on
dma 2 fails.  With Open Firmware the ISA driver is registered only when a
port parameter is given.

The internal speaker stays silent, only line/headphone out play. The
firmware sound package audio-init-setup programs I26 = 0x80 (mono
output MOUT unmuted) and ends with

  au-pin-ctl-reg au-iar!  au-idr aud@ 0x40 or au-idr!  0x96 ms

raising the I10 external control pin XCTL0 and waiting 150ms for the
speaker amplifier. The CS4236B data sheet describes MOUT as the drive
for the PC-internal mono speaker, while wss_lib keeps I10 at 0 apart
from IEN and mutes MOUT (I26 0xcf). Raise XCTL0 and unmute MOUT for
IBM0017 sound nodes and expose XCTL0 as "Speaker Playback Switch".

The XCTL0/XCTL1 definitions were swapped against the CS4231A and
CS4236B data sheets (I10 D6 = XCTL0, D7 = XCTL1), correct them and add
the I26 mono control bits.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

